  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting decent work for sustainable rural livelihoods with focus on the protection and empowerment of vulnerable populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Country Programme Outcome (CPO) supports efforts to improve working conditions and expand employment opportunities in rural Zambia. The interventions is promoting sustainable livelihoods by helping people access productive, inclusive, and resilient economic opportunities that can improve their living standards and contribute to local development. Further, focusing on increasing access to decent jobs, skills development, entrepreneurship, and better working conditions in sectors such as agriculture, forestry, fisheries, and small-scale enterprises. It is targeting vulnerable groups, including women, young people, Persons with Disabilities, and other marginalized groups, by improving their access to productive resources, markets and sustainable incomes. Through support for inclusive policies, stronger institutions, and sustainable livelihood initiatives, the intervention is contributing to poverty reduction, greater economic resilience, and more inclusive rural development. The programme is implemented in collaboration with government ministries, local communities, beneficiaries, and non-state actors.</narrative>
  </description>
